  "title": "Rocket Motion.",
  "body": " Rocket Motion   A rocket lifting off from a launch pad in Florida has a vertical position given by during the first moments of takeoff, where is the height of the rocket in meters and is the time in seconds after the rocket clears the support tower. Assuming the motion of the rocket is purely vertical, determine both the speed and the acceleration of the rocket at time .   "
