  "title": "Why you will do badly on tests if you don’t show all work.",
  "body": " Why you will do badly on tests if you don't show all work   A 3.5 meter long piece of rope has a mass of 250 g. Your goal is to determine the mass of a 7.0 meter long piece of the same rope.  Do this calculation in your head and then write down the answer on your paper.  Do this calculation again, but write down the steps and your reasoning on the paper.  Scribble out or erase every number and unit for parts (a) and (b). Now grade your work from parts (a) and (b) on a 0 10 point scale for each, basing the grade on how well someone could understand what you did and why from whatever remains visible on the page after the numbers and units have been erased or scribbled out.     "
